  "drafting_notes": "AUDIENCE: Year 1-2 (ages 6-8). Short everyday frames, home and school. Australian register: school terms, summer in January.\nEVERY frame must carry an explicit rate the child can count: 'every single time', 'most mornings', 'once or twice all year', 'not even once', 'some days yes and some days no'. A habit with no stated rate fits several of these words and will be rejected by the judges.\nTHE LADDER runs 0% to 100%: never < rarely < sometimes < usually < always. The stated rate must land clearly on ONE rung: 'not even once' = never; 'only once or twice a year' = rarely; 'some days yes, some days no' = sometimes; 'most days, but not all' = usually; 'every single time, without fail' = always.\nSLOTS: place the blank where all five adverbs scan: before the main verb ('She ___ walks to school') or after is/are ('He is ___ first to finish').\nSURFACES: adverbs; the surface form of every candidate is the word itself, unchanged, in every frame.",
